  "enhanced_information": "Ground glass hepatocytes are primarily associated with chronic hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection. This histological finding indicates abnormal protein accumulation due to the presence of viral antigens within the hepatocytes, which is characteristic of HBV. While ground glass hepatocytes can be seen in other liver conditions, they are most commonly linked to chronic HBV, with less frequent occurrences in hepatitis C or other types of hepatitis. Therefore, the most accurate option is chronic hepatitis by HBV."
